General information for Version fe56ib26                          2631 1451   30
                                                                  2631 1451   31
The file has been assembled at the IAEA and nicknamed             2631 1451   32
'fe56ib26'. It consists of:                                       2631 1451   33
- EMPIRE calculation "ib23" (Gforge repository No.529)            2631 1451   34
- Resolved resonance range up to 850 keV basically from JENDL-4.0 2631 1451   35
  (Froehner evaluation for JEF-2-2 with corrections for typos).   2631 1451   36
  The resonance energy at 766.7 kev was corrected.                2631 1451   37
  The p-wave resonance at 59.5 keV was removed.                   2631 1451   38
  The background near 800 keV was reduced by 40 percent.          2631 1451   39
  Artificial "background" was added to capture around 24.5 keV,   2631 1451   40
  since capture in the hole of the elastic seems to be low and is 2631 1451   41
  HIGHLY SENSITIVE to many benchmarks. It was stipulated that the 2631 1451   42
  broad dip in this energy region is caused by inappropriately    2631 1451   43
  placed bound states. The adjusted capture cross section now     2631 1451   44
  nearly follows the 1/v behaviour.                               2631 1451   45
- The total cross sections above the resonance range were taken   2631 1451   46
  from JEFF-3.2, which is essentially the Vonach-Tagesen          2631 1451   47
  evaluation with superimposed fluctuations that correspond       2631 1451   48
  to Berthold measurements on Fe-nat. The contribution of the     2631 1451   49
  minor isotopes is taken into account.                           2631 1451   50
- The capture cross sections above 860 keV were taken from the    2631 1451   51
  RPI data presented by Y. Danon at the ND2016 Conference.        2631 1451   52
- JEFF-3.2 contains inelastic cross sections measured by Dupont   2631 1451   53
  et al., but the authors discovered normalisation problems and   2631 1451   54
  the results were not published. New measurements were           2631 1451   55
  performed by Negret, but with a lower resolution. The Dupont    2631 1451   56
  and Negret data were binned over a suitable energy mesh.        2631 1451   57
  A piecewise linear scaling parameter was constructed to adjust  2631 1451   58
  Dupont data such that they agree on average with the Negret     2631 1451   59
  data. It was also found that the energy calibration of Negret   2631 1451   60
  data did not match the resonances of the total cross section.   2631 1451   61
  A correction was made to the energy scale which amounted to     2631 1451   62
  2.5 keV at 1.8 MeV.                                             2631 1451   63
  The Dupond-Negret data are applied up to 3.5e6 eV.              2631 1451   64
  In addition, the inelastic cross section below 1 MeV was        2631 1451   65
  reduced by 15 percent to approximately agree with Perey data.   2631 1451   66
- The (n,p) partial cross sections are re-scaled to match         2631 1451   67
  the total (n,p) cross section in the IRDFF-v1.05 file.          2631 1451   68
- The elastic cross section is defined as the difference between  2631 1451   69
  the total and the remaining partial cross sections. To test the 2631 1451   70
  consistency, the cross section was resolution-broadened to      2631 1451   71
  0.3 percent, achieving good agreement with Kinney data.         2631 1451   72
- The elastic angular distributions in the resolved resonance     2631 1451   73
  range are taken from resolution-broadened Perey data.           2631 1451   74
  Above the resonance range the angular distributions are taken   2631 1451   75
  from Kinney up to 2.2 MeV and from Skith up to 4 MeV.           2631 1451   76
  Above this energy they are taken from the Empire calculation.   2631 1451   77
