 CROSS-SECTION EVALUATION PROCEDURE                               2631 1451   93
                                                                  2631 1451   94
 Adopted procedure is based on careful theoretical                2631 1451   95
 analysis utilizing available experimental data and               2631 1451   96
 nuclear reaction model calculations.                             2631 1451   97
                                                                  2631 1451   98
 This code integrates into a single system a number               2631 1451   99
 of important modules and features:                               2631 1451  100
                                                                  2631 1451  101
 - Spherical and deformed Optical Model including                 2631 1451  102
   coupled-channels code ECIS06 by J. Raynal                      2631 1451  103
 - Soft-rotator deformed Optical Model including                  2631 1451  104
   coupled-channels code OPTMAN by E.Soukhovitskii                2631 1451  105
   and coworkers                                                  2631 1451  106
 - Hauser-Feshbach statistical model including                    2631 1451  107
   width fluctuation correction, and the                          2631 1451  108
   optical model for fission with partial damping                 2631 1451  109
 - Quantum-mechanical MSD TUL model (codes ORION &                2631 1451  110
   TRISTAN by H.Lenske), and MSC NVWY model                       2631 1451  111
 - Exciton model with Iwamoto-Harada cluster                      2631 1451  112
   emission and Kalbach systematic angular distr.                 2631 1451  113
   (code PCROSS by R.Capote et al)                                2631 1451  114
 - Hybrid Monte Carlo preequilibrium model(M.Blann)               2631 1451  115
   (code DDHMS by M.Chadwick, mod. by B.V.Carlson)                2631 1451  116
 - Complete gamma-ray cascade after emission of                   2631 1451  117
   each particle, including realistic treatment of                2631 1451  118
   discrete transitions                                           2631 1451  119
 - Access to OM segment of the RIPL library [RIPL]                2631 1451  120
 - Built-in input parameter files, such as masses,                2631 1451  121
   level density, discrete levels, fission barriers               2631 1451  122
   and gamma strength functions based on the RIPL                 2631 1451  123
   library [RIPL]                                                 2631 1451  124
 - Automatic retrieval of experimental data from the              2631 1451  125
   EXFOR library                                                  2631 1451  126
 - ENDF-6 formatting (code EMPEND by A.Trkov)                     2631 1451  127
   coupled to graphical presentation capabilities                 2631 1451  128
   (code ZVView by V. Zerkin) through the chain of                2631 1451  129
   PrePro codes by D. Cullen                                      2631 1451  130
 - ENDF checking codes (CHECKR, FIZCON, PSYCHE)                   2631 1451  131
 - Highly automated fitting of optical model                      2631 1451  132
   parameters (by B.V. Carlson)                                   2631 1451  133
 - KALMAN code for fitting experimental data and                  2631 1451  134
 - generating covariances                                         2631 1451  135
 - Support for NJOY                                               2631 1451  136
